{
  "_comment": [
    "SHARED cross-language fixture for THE count predicate (sprint-18 C4, bd polyglot-pdf-g687).",
    "",
    "Consumed by BOTH schema-editor/src/utils/reviewStatus.parity.test.ts (running the real",
    "isCountedReviewed) and backend/tests/unit/test_publish_readiness.py (running the real",
    "is_counted_reviewed). Every case must produce the SAME boolean on both sides.",
    "",
    "This file exists because a mirror pinned only by prose drifted: the Python side omitted",
    "the guidance-staleness exclusion from the timeliness rule, so the ordinary",
    "sign-off -> drift -> ack flow counted reviewed in the editor and NOT reviewed in the",
    "stamp -- one saved kit, two numbers, which is the exact bug this bead exists to end",
    "(Opus fresh-eyes round 2). Per-side unit tests could not catch it; only a shared",
    "expectation can.",
    "",
    "ADD A CASE whenever either predicate gains or changes a clause. `ackSha1: \"@identity\"`",
    "is a placeholder each side replaces with the field's own natively-computed identity",
    "hash (the two languages compute it differently but must agree on the value).",
    "",
    "NOT COVERED, and provably UNCOVERABLE: 'a checkbox_group wrongly sets suppress_unmapped_scan'. That flag is unreachable for checkbox_group by construction -- the stray-field-level-name rule returns True before it is consulted, so the mutation is behaviourally inert and NO fixture case can redden on it. A case added for that dimension looks like coverage and is not; one was added and removed after the mutation stayed green (bd polyglot-pdf-sqkii)."
  ],
